   "edited": false,
   "license": "CC BY-SA 2.5",
   "body_html": "@Erik: I think as far as memory checkers go, the memory allocated by the <code>malloc()</code> call would be associated with the <code>realloc()</code> call. So technically, as far as memory checkers go, only <code>realloc()</code> leaked (again, I&#39;m just guessing). I believe this is because <code>realloc()</code> may not be able to just extend the already allocated memory chunk in size due to memory fragmentation. Instead, it may have to release the memory and allocate a totally new chunk of the requested size."
