  {
   "post_type": "answer",
   "post_id": 14463624,
   "parent_id": 5339282,
   "author_user_id": 2001035,
   "author_display_name": "arodmon",
   "author_id_missing": false,
   "role": "responder",
   "is_accepted": false,
   "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/a/14463624",
   "score": 0,
   "created_utc": "2013-01-22T16:43:51Z",
   "last_edit_utc": null,
   "last_activity_utc": "2013-01-22T16:43:51Z",
   "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
   "body_html": "<p>You create strfree() function and it is not used inside the code.\nThe memory need to be free always, if it is not used.</p>\n\n<pre><code>if (!tmp) {\n    printf(\"failure\");\n    if (!(*s) &amp;&amp; !((*s)-&gt;buf))\n       strfree(&amp;(*s));\n    exit(-1);\n}\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>Looking strfree(), looks as you reserved memory for *s too in somewhere.\nDo the same before your code finish.</p>\n\n<pre><code>if (!(*s) &amp;&amp; !((*s)-&gt;buf))\n   strfree(&amp;(*s));\n</code></pre>\n"
  },
  {
   "post_type": "comment",
   "post_id": 20170819,
   "parent_id": 5339282,
   "parent_type": "question",
   "author_user_id": 146377,
   "author_display_name": "Patrick Schlüter",
   "author_id_missing": false,
   "role": "responder",
   "is_accepted": null,
   "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/5339282/#comment20170819_5339282",
   "score": 0,
   "created_utc": "2013-01-23T10:53:01Z",
   "edited": false,
   "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
   "body_html": "You don&#39;t need the double indirection <code>**s</code> in <code>strnappnd</code> as you never change the pointer itself only the structure it points to. This will allow to remove all the unecessary <code>(*p)</code> indirections."
  },
  {
